# Corpus seed fixtures are copied BYTE-FOR-BYTE into a target repo, so their line
# endings are part of the fixture, not a checkout detail. Without this, a Windows
# checkout under `core.autocrlf=true` would seed CRLF files while a Linux checkout
# seeds LF ones — the same corpus measuring two different premises depending on who
# ran it. `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion in both directions.
#
# See docs/gotchas/worker-eol-nondeterministic-for-crlf-proof.md for why EOL in this
# codebase is never assumed and always pinned.
* -text
